rpt":"Fried Chicken Nirvana. I have to give credit to Ian McNulty from the Advocate for his best gas station fried chicken article directing me to this place. Friendly neighborhood folks abound as you wait for fresh tenders (4 and fries for 4.99 or 8 for 5.99). They are plump juicy spicy slightly greasy in a good way. Unlike other tenders Ive had in the past these are succulent with the flavor profile of bone-in fried chicken with a hint of skin in the crunchy parts. The bone-in breasts are 1.79 and so flavorful and satisfying. I pick it as clean as ant pile would. The fries are nothing special, but regular old food service fries are the perfect compliment to any good chicken. The huge po boys ..."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
